# pi (pi-subagents) layer: what differs from the tool-neutral subagents/<name>.md for pi (pi-subagents).
# One line per setting: <agent> <key> <value>. Each becomes a frontmatter line
# `key: value` in the generated file. setup/subagents.sh applies it.
# model: a pi model id or a fuzzy name such as sonnet or opus. tools: pi built-ins
# (read, bash, edit, write, grep, find, ls); Glob is find. WebFetch and WebSearch have no
# pi built-in, and the YNAB MCP tools are not listed for finance-analyst: pi-mcp-adapter
# supplies tools through extensions, which an agent inherits by default.

accessibility-tester model sonnet
accessibility-tester tools read, grep, find, bash
andrew-voice-writer model opus
andrew-voice-writer tools read, write, edit, find, grep
architect-reviewer model opus
architect-reviewer tools read, grep, find, bash
code-reviewer model opus
code-reviewer tools read, grep, find, bash
csharp-developer model sonnet
csharp-developer tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
debugger model opus
debugger tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
electron-pro model sonnet
electron-pro tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
finance-analyst model sonnet
finance-analyst tools read, write
performance-engineer model sonnet
performance-engineer tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
powershell-expert model sonnet
powershell-expert tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
react-specialist model sonnet
react-specialist tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
refactoring-specialist model sonnet
refactoring-specialist tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
research-analyst model sonnet
research-analyst tools read, grep, find
security-auditor model opus
security-auditor tools read, grep, find
technical-writer model sonnet
technical-writer tools read, write, edit, find, grep
test-automator model sonnet
test-automator tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
typescript-pro model sonnet
typescript-pro tools read, write, edit, bash, find, grep
